    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d919">

                <pb facs="0719" n="603" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg603"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13384.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Secretary of War.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your letter of September 21 in regard to the exaction of further
                    payments [etc.]</p>
                <pb facs="0720" n="604" xml:id="pg604"/>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to enclose herewith, for your information, a copy of a
                    telegram which the Department despatched on September 22 to the Brazilian
                    Minister at Mexico City in connection with these matters.</p>
                <p>The Department will be glad to take up the other matters mentioned in your letter
                    when a reply is received from the Brazilian Minister.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <p>For the Secretary of State,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
